%% Fast Session — Madar V1
%% Authority: Descriptive. Source of truth: docs/05-runtime/fast-session.md
sequenceDiagram
    actor Teacher
    participant App as Web/API (Fast Session)
    participant DB as Persistence
    participant W as Worker
    participant Push as Push (external)

    Teacher->>App: open group session (Planned -> Open)
    loop per student
        Teacher->>App: tap Present/Absent (or Studied/Not-Studied/Skip)
        App->>DB: persist record per-tap
        alt Absent or Not-Studied
            App->>DB: record + notification EVENT (same transaction)
        else Skip
            Note over App: no record, no event
        end
        App-->>Teacher: advance to next student (no wait)
    end
    Teacher->>App: close session (Open -> Closed)
    W->>DB: read pending notification events
    W->>Push: deliver (async; may fail independently)
    Note over Teacher,DB: Correction: Closed->Reopened->flip->re-persist->Closed;<br/>prior notification not retracted; new Absent may fire new event
